{"RunId":"0e6834cd-9d6c-415b-b030-2e4e1616b9fa","Seq":30,"Kind":"NodeCompleted","Synthetic":true,"TimestampUtc":"2026-04-25T00:48:58.2698828Z","NodeId":"n_ym05bcg","NodeName":null,"Payload":{"nodeInstanceId":"33d16885-7a01-48d8-b298-3b5cad0b26ff","duration":"PT1M27.2320464S","inputData":{"triggerType":"WebHook","triggerTime":"2026-04-25T00:47:31.0096349Z","webHookMethod":"POST","webHookRoute":"/webhook/investigate-icm","bodyJsonSchema":"{\n   \u0022type\u0022: \u0022object\u0022,\n   \u0022required\u0022: [\u0022incidentId\u0022, \u0022serviceName\u0022, \u0022teamName\u0022, \u0022timestamp\u0022],\n   \u0022properties\u0022: {\n     \u0022incidentId\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022integer\u0022, \u0022format\u0022: \u0022int64\u0022 },\n     \u0022serviceName\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022string\u0022 },\n     \u0022teamName\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022string\u0022 },\n     \u0022timestamp\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022string\u0022, \u0022format\u0022: \u0022date-time\u0022 }\n   }\n }","messageType":"json","body.timestamp":"2026-04-25T00:47:18.610Z","body.incidentId":783872773,"body.serviceName":"","body.teamName":"","__webhookBody":"{\n  \u0022incidentId\u0022: 783872773 ,\n  \u0022serviceName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022teamName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022timestamp\u0022: \u00222026-04-25T00:47:18.610Z\u0022\n}"},"outputData":{"mode":"skill","backend":"copilot","model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","agentName":"open-icm","agentSummary":"","result":"Based on the extracted incident data, here\u0027s my analysis:\n\n---\n\n## ICM 783872773 \u2014 Investigation Report\n\n### \uD83D\uDCCB Incident Overview\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **ID** | 783872773 |\n| **Severity** | Sev 3 |\n| **Status** | Active |\n| **Service** | Azure Stack HCI / Arc Managed VMs |\n| **Owner** | Michael Duppr\u00E9 (mduppre) |\n| **Region** | USGOVVirginia |\n| **Cluster** | \u0060ceo-clu001\u0060 (subscription \u0060f726effd-d97f-48c1-8f47-e0bb67d2fe33\u0060) |\n\n---\n\n### \uD83D\uDD0D Root Cause\n\n**Webhook validation incorrectly fires on NIC deletion due to an IP range conflict introduced during an OS upgrade.**\n\n1. Customer deployed Azure Local **2512**, created \u0060LNET1-Static\u0060 with IP pool containing \u006010.10.35.52\u0060 and \u006010.10.35.61\u0060\n2. After upgrading to **2601**, the platform automatically created a new infra LNET: \u0060ceo-clu001-Infra-LNET\u0060 \u2014 with an **overlapping IP range**\n3. When the customer tried to delete the orphaned NIC \u0060arcvm001-NIC\u0060 (left over after VM deletion via portal), the admission webhook rejected the request:\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\ncreateupdatevalidationwebhook.infrastructure.azstackhci.microsoft.com denied the request:\nThe following IP Pool ranges you entered are already in use:\n[10.10.35.52, 10.10.35.61] by ceo-clu001-InfraLNET.\nPlease choose different ranges to avoid conflicts.\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\nThe validation webhook is **incorrectly triggering IP conflict checks on a DELETE operation**, which should not require IP range validation. This is the core bug \u2014 \u0060createupdatevalidation\u0060 webhook should skip IP pool conflict checks when the operation is a deletion.\n\n---\n\n### \uD83D\uDCA5 Impact\n\n- **Scope**: Internal test stamp only \u2014 no customer-facing or production impact\n- **Functional block**: Customer cannot clean up orphaned NIC resource after VM deletion\n- **Secondary ask**: Customer also wants to recreate the LNET after resolving the IP overlap\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Recommended Next Steps\n\n#### Immediate Mitigation\n1. **Manual deletion via kubectl/ARM**: Bypass the webhook by directly deleting the NIC resource using \u0060kubectl delete networkinterfaces arcvm001-NIC -n \u003Cnamespace\u003E\u0060 on the cluster, or via a direct ARM \u0060DELETE\u0060 call from the backend (bypassing the admission webhook).\n2. **Resolve the IP overlap**: Remove or update \u0060ceo-clu001-Infra-LNET\u0060 to use a non-overlapping IP range, which would allow normal portal deletion to succeed.\n\n#### Bug Fix (Engineering)\n3. **Fix the admission webhook** (\u0060createupdatevalidationwebhook\u0060): IP pool conflict validation must be **skipped for DELETE operations** on NetworkInterface resources. The validator should only run on CREATE/UPDATE.\n4. **Investigate upgrade path**: The 2512\u21922601 upgrade creating an infra LNET with overlapping IPs is a secondary bug \u2014 upgrade should detect existing LNETs and choose non-conflicting IP ranges for infra LNETs.\n\n#### Long-term\n5. File a bug on the webhook logic to guard against IP range validation on deletions.\n6. Add upgrade-path logic to detect and warn about LNET IP conflicts before auto-creating infra LNETs.\n\n---\n\n### \uD83D\uDDC2 Output\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n[OUTPUT:incidentFolder] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\n[OUTPUT:summary.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\summary.md\n[OUTPUT:discussion.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\discussion.md\n[OUTPUT:rca.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\rca.md\n[OUTPUT:metadata.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\metadata.md\n[OUTPUT:ai_summary.md] \n\u0060\u0060\u0060","ai.success":true,"ai.model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","ai.durationMs":80437,"ai.inputTokens":243387,"ai.outputTokens":2635,"incidentFolder":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773","summary.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\summary.md","discussion.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\discussion.md","rca.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\rca.md","metadata.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\metadata.md"},"globalVariables":{"maxQueryScore":0,"body.timestamp":"2026-04-25T00:47:18.610Z","codeIssueFile":"","__webhookBody":"{\n  \u0022incidentId\u0022: 783872773 ,\n  \u0022serviceName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\